WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.355
The secret language that we all
speak means every bit of nonverbal

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:26.480
communication that we use to interact
with other people in our relationships.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.550
The interesting thing is that
we are all experts in it.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.250
Everybody that walks into every lecture
that I give is already an expert.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.710
Just navigating the line at coffee and
traffic, and

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.780
walking on public transit, you're
speaking that language in negotiating.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.690
Who moves out of the way?

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.190
What gestures do you do,
and who takes what seat?

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.768
It's all communicating in
this language of power.

00:00:54.768 --> 00:00:59.520
An example, a cocktail party,
there's a circle of people,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.550
they're standing around talking and
someone starts to approach.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.870
That circle of people is
either going to open up and

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.180
invite that person in or
it's going to close ranks a little,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.650
because it's not, for whatever reason,
okay for that person to enter.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:18.800
The conversation needs to go a particular
way because of who that person is,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.670
whatever the context.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.490
That's happens all the time,

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.520
it happens in bars and
in coffee houses everywhere we go.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.175
So, that's also communicating
in this languages of power and

00:01:30.175 --> 00:01:32.300
it's something we don't think about,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.940
the group doesn't have a vote on how
we're going to behave, they just react.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.122
And it's six or seven people
reacting to small verbal cues,

00:01:42.122 --> 00:01:45.321
small nonverbal cues, all simultaneously.

00:01:45.321 --> 00:01:50.463
[MUSIC]

00:01:50.463 --> 00:01:54.384
Any one individual can change
the dynamic of the group or

00:01:54.384 --> 00:01:58.651
the person they're with and
they do it by a set of behaviors.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:03.322
What we're talking about is the difference
between being more authoritative or

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:05.180
being more approachable.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:09.800
So, if you want to join the circle,
you can enter the circle

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.570
before you even approach it by
calling out someone's name and

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.650
that puts you inside that circle already.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:22.930
You could come up and tap someone on
the shoulder, or gently nudge someone, and

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:28.030
all of that nonverbal
communication is asserting,

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.040
I'm here, I'm taking an authoritative
approach that I'm going to enter.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.290
It's a little on
the dominant side of things.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.890
Conversely, if you're in the circle,

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.360
you can decide I'm going to
let that person in.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.470
You can use your power from within
the circle and take up this space and

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:51.670
say, I own this and
because I do, come and join me.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.495
Come into my space,
I'm holding in the circle here, and

00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:58.774
I'm going to let you in and
share my power with you.

00:02:58.774 --> 00:03:03.651
[MUSIC]

00:03:03.651 --> 00:03:07.480
I typically show up with
a little bit more emotion.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.600
My head's a little to the side,
and I tend to be friendly.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.840
In fact, people come up on the street and
ask me questions all over the world,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.480
when I'm not local, directions, or
other things, because I'm that way.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:26.340
But I can change by just making my self a
little more still, a little more upright,

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.710
I can make my voice go a little
bit lower into my chest voice.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:37.390
I can speak a little bit more slowly and

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:42.140
I can leave more space in my words and
slow down my gestures.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:47.680
Now, I would say across
that last 30 seconds,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.580
I became a lot more grounded and
authoritative, and you would

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:57.020
believe the directions I was giving you
in London, even if I didn't know them.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:02.460
Conversely, if that's
how you always show up,

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:08.310
if you tend to be in this slow place,
you can make small changes.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.590
You can talk just a little bit faster,
maybe you can tilt your head a little bit,

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.530
you can nod.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.750
Maybe touch your chin a little bit
as you talk or a little bit more

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:24.130
gesture with your hand and I think this is
a little friendlier, it's a little softer.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:29.235
Just by making those small changes,
two things happen.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:35.700
One, I'm communicating to you
a different set of social cues,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.070
about that you can approach me or
that you shouldn't and

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:45.750
as it turns out, by changing your
body you change your internal state.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.613
In one place where I'm more authoritative,

00:04:48.613 --> 00:04:53.297
I will begin to feel more authoritative
just by taking on those gestures.

00:04:53.297 --> 00:04:55.897
And I will feel a little more friendly and

00:04:55.897 --> 00:04:59.360
approachable by taking on
the other set of gestures.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.620
So it works both ways.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.971
You can decide to be it inside and
it will come out naturally and

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:09.167
you can decide to put it on physically and
it will go inside.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:14.165
[MUSIC]

00:05:14.165 --> 00:05:16.730
After you start thinking about this,
you can't avoid it.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:20.840
You'll see it as you walk across campus or
as you go to get a coffee.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.800
But it's the just
the background that's happening

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.100
because it's naturally how we communicate.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.430
You don't have to make strategic choices
all day long, that would be exhausting.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.578
But most of us have learned
this navigation as children and

00:05:34.578 --> 00:05:37.788
as we come up and we sort a lot
of it out in junior high school,

00:05:37.788 --> 00:05:42.000
it's all these social cues and
it's just how we function in the world.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.740
So we're on autopilot most of the time and
that works great for

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.240
90% of the people, there are a few.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.942
But it works great all the time.

00:05:52.942 --> 00:05:55.940
When it's really important,
when it makes a difference,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.770
you might want to consider
some different choices.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.900
When it is an important meeting for
you, when it isn't going well,

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:06.130
when you are having a challenging
situation, these are the points where you

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.770
might want to stop and take a thought and
a little bit of action.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.660
And then you can go
back to just being you.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.944
Because most of us are successful,
well-adjusted people that

00:06:16.944 --> 00:06:20.124
navigate this without thinking and
that's how it should be.

00:06:20.124 --> 00:06:25.228
[MUSIC]

00:06:25.228 --> 00:06:29.598
Often, when we come home from a stressful
day and we walk in the house,

00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:31.760
we carry all of that along with us.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.350
It just comes along because
that commute was rough and

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:40.170
that guy cut us off and
all of that's inside and

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.410
as I said, what's inside comes out,
and so we walk in the house.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:50.940
But you can stop right at the door and
take 30 seconds or a minute and reset.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.580
Think about what's on
the other side of the door.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:54.730
How much you care about them.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.840
How you want to show up for them.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:03.170
What fun you have had and are planning to
have and that will start to change you.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.960
You could put a smile on and
change your body and

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.770
then when you walk through the door,
you're a different you.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.290
Everybody's fear, primarily,

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:21.750
is that the way that they are isn't
the way that they should be.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.390
What if I was the other
side of the equation?

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:30.170
And then, most people are afraid
of actually being powerful.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.430
They say they're not.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.920
Our students come in, and
they act in powerful ways, but

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.980
when we push them to really step into it,
it's a challenge.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:48.640
There are a number of poems and
songs that are all written about this, but

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.200
the thing that we're really most
afraid of is being powerful.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:58.580
To stand in a very confident, really stand
in your power is a scary place to be.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.230
And if you can do that then
you can change the world,

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.180
you can change the people around you.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:09.350
You can lead people to do things and
accomplish your goals and

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:11.040
it's an incredible place to be.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:18.560
When I coach someone, and they step
into their power the first time ever,

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.308
they have a visceral reaction.

00:08:20.308 --> 00:08:24.310
It's an emotional experience and
they feel incredible and

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:28.960
it's frightening and exciting and
scaring at the same time.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.546
The secret, the thing that they all want
to know, is how to stand in that place and

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:34.568
be comfortable.

00:08:34.568 --> 00:08:39.069
[MUSIC]

